## Summary

Shipped `RouteAnnouncer` — the native SwiftUI parity of `web/src/components/a11y/RouteAnnouncer.tsx` — as 11 files (commit `5699d1468`, +2,113 lines), decomposed per the established shared-surface architecture (Adapter / Model / Seams / Views / States / main View / Previews / strings + 3 test files).

**Parity reproduced from the web source** (not the templated prompt metadata): watch route changes (`useLocation`), defer the page-title read, voice it politely to VoiceOver, **skip the first paint**, **rotate a 0–3 zero-width-space suffix** so duplicate titles re-announce, **clear on empty title**, and **cancel a pending announcement** when the route changes again. Presented as a visible inspector (live-region card + recent-announcement log) with every P4 leaf state (loading/empty/error/data + stale/offline), bound through `RouteAnnouncerModel` (P1/S8), strings via the P1/S10 facade, tokens via P1/S9, `view.opened` telemetry via P1/S11. No view-level networking; no `TODO`/stub/placeholder.

